@section ActionDescription {
    <p>
        This example visualizes monthly global climate signals during 2025
        using temperature anomaly, atmospheric CO₂, and Arctic sea ice extent
        data. Multiple axes are used to compare measurements with different
        units and value ranges in a single chart.
    </p>
}

@section Description {
    <p>
        The chart demonstrates how unrelated datasets with different value
        ranges can be plotted together to provide a unified view of climate
        signals.
    </p>

    <p>
        In this example, the combination chart is configured with the following
        features:
    </p>

    <ul class="climate-feature-list">
        <li>
            An area series for Arctic sea ice extent on the outer-right Y axis.
        </li>
        <li>
            A line series for temperature anomalies on the primary Y axis.
        </li>
        <li>
            A spline series for atmospheric CO₂ on the inner-right Y axis.
        </li>
        <li>
            Distinct color-coded axes, labels, and legends for each measurement.
        </li>
        <li>
            Annotations that highlight the temperature anomaly peak, seasonal
            CO₂ peak, and annual sea ice minimum.
        </li>
    </ul>

    <p>
        <code>Tooltip</code> and <code>Crosshair</code> are enabled in this
        example. Hover over a point or tap on one on touch-enabled devices to
        display the shared tooltip. Move the pointer along the chart to track
        values across all three axes.
    </p>

    <p>
        More information about multiple axes can be found in this
        <a
            target="_blank"
            href="https://ej2.syncfusion.com/aspnetcore/documentation/chart/axis-customization#multiple-axis">
            documentation section
        </a>.
    </p>
}

@section Title {
    <title>
        ASP.NET Core Chart Multi-Axis Combination Example - Syncfusion Demos
    </title>
}

@section Header {
    <h1 class="sb-sample-text">
        Example of Multi-Axis Combination Chart in ASP.NET Core Chart Control
    </h1>
}